[[10880,4181,"No review of the decision to discharge was sought or conducted when it became apparent that there had been a material change in Susan's presentation on the 10th November. Had a review taken place then it is likely that the discharge would have been deferred or cancelled.","discharge without review",""],[10881,4181,"The discharge process was disjointed, lacked co-ordination and did not involve Susan's Primary/Associate Nurse.","disjointed discharge process",""],[10882,4181,"The Discharge Policy was perfunctory and staff failed to follow it in any event.","perfunctory discharge policy",""],[10883,4181,"Poor record keeping, predominantly on the part of the nursing staff.","poor record keeping",""],[10884,4181,"There is no protocol/guidance on what steps should be taken when an inpatient contacts the emergency services (e.g. police via 999).","absence of emergency contact protocol",""],[10885,4181,"Unprofessional staff attitudes towards patient/care provision - two qualified nurses involved in Susan's care used inappropriate language and demonstrated negative ways of thinking during both conversations with colleagues and the police communications operator.","unprofessional staff attitudes",""]]